# OPDP stream

Import ProblemRecord from "./problem_record.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import RankScore from "./rank_score.lg".
Import WireRead from "./wire_read.lg".
Import OpdpRow from "./opdp_row.lg".
Import AtlasGraph from "./atlas_graph.lg".
Import OpdpProfile from "./opdp_profile.lg".
Import OpdpImportRules from "./opdp_import_rules.lg".
Import LoadRules from "./load_rules.lg".

One atlas record projected once into the rows it adds: the problem and its rank
through the factory's own `opdp_row.lg` and `atlas_graph.lg`, the nodes of the
graph above it (cohort, source collection, category, parents first), its own node,
and its profile (`opdp_profile.lg`). The rows are small and returned by value;
the batch they join is the caller's.

## A RecordRows has:
    a problem, which is Text.
    an innerIds, which is Seq of Text.
    an inner, which is Seq of Text.
    a leaf, which is Text.
    a profile, which is Text.
    a ranked, which is Bool.

## Note
The rows of one parsed record, under the cohort its dataset version names. A
record without the scores the scheduler reads is still imported, ranked as an
unprofiled problem of its category, and counted.

## To projectRecord (v: Json, cohortLabels: Map of Text to Text) -> RecordRows:
    Let category be slugOr(v, "classification.category").
    Let mutable inputs be unprofiledInputs("informal", category).
    Let mutable ranked be true.
    Inspect opdpRankInputs(v):
        When Ok (r):
            Set inputs to r.
        When Err (e):
            Set ranked to false.
    Let cohort be cohortKeyOf(textAt(jsonGet(v, "implementation"), "dataset_version")).
    Let row be opdpRowFrom(v, cohort, inputs).
    Let mutable p be row's problem.
    Set p's cohort to cohort.
    Let rank be rowRank(row).
    Let cohortId be cohortNodeId(cohort).
    Let collectionId be collectionNodeId(cohort, row's collectionSlug).
    Let categoryId be categoryNodeId(cohort, row's collectionSlug, row's categorySlug).
    Let mutable cohortLabel be cohort.
    If cohortLabels contains cohort:
        Set cohortLabel to item cohort of cohortLabels.
    Let n1 be toJson_Node(rankedNode(cohortId, none, none, "cohort", cohortLabel, rank)).
    Let n2 be toJson_Node(rankedNode(collectionId, some cohortId, none, "collection", row's collectionLabel, rank)).
    Let n3 be toJson_Node(rankedNode(categoryId, some collectionId, none, "category", row's categoryLabel, rank)).
    Let mutable out be a new RecordRows with problem toJson_Problem(p) and innerIds [cohortId, collectionId, categoryId] and inner [n1, n2, n3].
    Set out's leaf to toJson_Node(rankedNode(problemNodeId(p's id), some categoryId, some p's id, "problem", p's title, rank)).
    Set out's profile to "{{\"id\":" + jsonQuote(p's id) + ",\"p\":" + opdpProfile(v) + "}}".
    Set out's ranked to ranked.
    Return out.
